<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qana (Yemen)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Qani', Qana (Hadramawt)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qana was the main port of the ancient Kingdom of Hadramawt, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a> coast of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> near modern Bir Ali. Frankincense from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhofar">Dhofar</a> and the interior was collected there for shipment, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/periplus-of-the-erythraean-sea">Periplus of the Erythraean Sea</a> describes it in the 1st century CE. Excavations have found warehouses and pottery from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p></div>
